# Semgrep exclusions.
#
# Semgrep's own defaults still apply — this file adds to them rather than
# replacing them.

# build.php is a standalone command-line build script. It is never
# autoloaded, never routed to, and never shipped: the production zip it
# assembles does not contain it.
#
# It trips two rules that are entirely correct about web code and entirely
# beside the point here — `exec-use`, because it shells out to composer and
# to git, and `unlink-use`, because it cleans its own staging directory.
# Neither takes anything from a request, because nothing here ever sees a
# request.
#
# Excluded as a file rather than suppressed line by line, because every
# finding in it has the same answer and a dozen `nosemgrep` comments would
# only make the next person read the reasoning a dozen times. Reach ships
# the same script; its findings were triaged in the Semgrep platform
# instead, which works but is not visible in the repository.
build.php
